      "classification": "validated_extension",
      "source_classification": "validated_extension",
      "statement": "A continuous two-slope salinity relation with a thermal endmember correction improves held-cast CDOM prediction. It is compatible with changing water-mass mixtures across a halocline. CDOM fluorescence does not independently measure chemical DOC, and the model cannot separate mixing, biology or photochemistry.",
      "applicability": "CDOM ppb is the publisher-calibrated fluorescence channel, not chemically measured DOC concentration. Quality control does not establish a universal conservative-mixing relationship. No target-based outlier removal.",
      "limitations": "All baselines and alternatives evaluated on identical frozen eligible observations; no confirmation promotion.",
      "falsification": "All baselines and alternatives evaluated on identical frozen eligible observations; no confirmation promotion.",
